{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And HaShem shut him in.</b> He had left the ark open, out of fear that perhaps not all had come, for he did not recognize every species among the creatures. And when they all came, <b>and HaShem shut him in</b> — the opening closed by itself by means of the wind, similar to what we find in Pesaḥim: the gates of the Temple courtyard, which were open, locked by themselves on the eve of Pesach. <b>[In front of him</b> — on his account.]"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:18.580017910Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}